    "type": "question",
    "label": "1",
    "prompt": "Find the value of $a$ and $b$ if\n$$\\left(\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{2}\\right)^4=a+b\\sqrt{6}.$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$a=49$, $b=20$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\n(\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{2})^4&=(\\sqrt{3})^4+4(\\sqrt{3})^3\\sqrt{2}+6(\\sqrt{3})^2(\\sqrt{2})^2+4\\sqrt{3}(\\sqrt{2})^3+(\\sqrt{2})^4\\\\\n(\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{2})^4&=9+12\\sqrt{6}+36+8\\sqrt{6}+4\\\\\n(\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{2})^4&=49+20\\sqrt{6}.\n\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore, $a=49$ and $b=20$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
